      "content": "Even with your past tetanus vaccination, a deep puncture wound from a rusty metal object carries a high risk of tetanus because the bacteria can survive for decades and your immune response might not be immediate; you likely need a booster shot within 48 hours to stay protected. Furthermore, signs of serious infection like \"gas gangrene\" can develop rapidly inside a deep puncture before redness or swelling even appear at the surface, making early professional evaluation crucial. Given the nature of the injury and the object used, attempting to treat this at home is unsafe, and you should seek medical care immediately rather than waiting to see if symptoms develop. Please go to urgent care or the ER now to rule out severe complications.",
